    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Spy Network', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 8, 'cost_text': '8 pts', 'tags': ['EoE'], 'effect': 'Access to an intelligence network. Once per OOC week, the spymaster designates one focus target from three categories. The network produces intelligence automatically each tick during the week based on the chosen focus. Daidoji pay 7 pts, Scorpion pay 6 pts, Kolat pay 5 pts.\nCharacter Focus: The network watches a specific named character. Each tick, one previously unknown fact about that character is revealed to the spymaster. Candidates include: current primary objective, a hidden disposition value toward a specific person, a concealed Disadvantage or Dark Secret, their actual Honor Rank (vs. perceived), or their current location. The engine selects the most relevant unrevealed fact based on the spymaster’s own active objective. Once all discoverable facts are exhausted, subsequent ticks yield no new information and the spymaster should reassign focus.\nPlace Focus: The network monitors a specific location (province, city, court, or castle). During the OOC week, any Tier 3 or Tier 4 topic generated at that location that the spymaster does not already know is revealed to them. One topic per tick, prioritized by recency. If no unknown topics were generated at that location during the week, no intelligence is produced.\nArmy Focus: The network tracks a specific enemy army. Once during the OOC week, the spymaster receives the army’s most recent known position on the world map, its approximate size (PU count), and the identity of its commander. If the army moved during the week, the position reported is the most recent one the network observed. Army focus does not reveal army composition, equipment tier, or morale: only position, size, and commander.\nNPC Trigger Rule: An NPC with Spy Network selects a focus target aligned with their current primary objective. Political objectives default to Character Focus on the most relevant rival or target. Military objectives default to Army Focus on the nearest or most threatening enemy force. Economic and territorial objectives default to Place Focus on the relevant province or trade hub. The focus is reassigned automatically when the NPC’s primary objective changes.'},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Stolen Identity', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 6, 'cost_text': '6 pts, 5 for Spider', 'tags': [], 'effect': 'Discovered the trappings of another life in the ruins of Otosan Uchi. Choose any family and School from another Great Clan plus an alias. Two Free Raises on Acting rolls when using this alternate identity. Gain the Outfit (not the koku) of the chosen School.'},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Strategist', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 5, 'cost_text': '5 pts', 'tags': ['S****&****F'], 'effect': "If serving as commander or senior subordinate commander of an army, or on the commander's staff: +2k0 to the Battle (Mass Combat)/Perception Roll to determine who is Winning each Battle Turn; +1k0 to any other Battle Skill Roll during a Mass Battle Turn. Lion pay 4 pts."},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Strength of the Earth', 'category': 'Physical', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'TN penalties from Wound Ranks are reduced by 3. Bushi pay 2 pts.'},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Student of Shourido', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 9, 'cost_text': '9 pts, 6 for Spider', 'tags': [], 'effect': 'When rolling to resist Temptation, Intimidation, or Fear, may add +5 to the roll instead of adding Honor Rank.'},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Tactician', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'When making a roll on the Mass Battle Table, may increase or decrease the result by 5. Lion and bushi pay 3 pts.'},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Touch of the Spirit Realms', 'category': 'Spiritual', 'points': 5, 'cost_text': '5 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': "A fragment of a spirit realm's essence is present in your soul. Shugenja pay 4 pts. Chikushudo: +1k1 to Animal Handling. Gaki-do: Killing an opponent immediately heals 5 Wounds. Jigoku: Add Taint Rank to attack rolls and Physical Trait rolls (requires possessing the Taint; Lost add twice Taint Rank). Maigo no Musha: +1 additional Glory point when awarded more than 3 points. Meido: +2k0 to Contested Rolls vs social manipulation. Sakkaku: +1k1 to Sincerity (Deceit). Tengoku: +2k0 to Earth Ring Rolls to resist Taint. Toshigoku: +5 feet to Move Actions toward an opponent (8 pts). Yomi: +1k0 to one selected School Skill (7 pts). Yume-do: Recover all Void Points with only 4 hours of rest."},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Virtuous', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Possess one additional Rank of Honor above normal starting value.'},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Voice', 'category': 'Physical', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': '+1k1 to any Perform Skill Roll utilizing the voice (Singing, Oratory, etc.).'},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Void Versatility', 'category': 'Spiritual', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': [], 'effect': 'Select one non-Void Ring. May expend spell slots associated with that Ring to cast Void spells. Only available to shugenja with Void Affinity.'},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Wary', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': '+1k1 to Investigation (Notice)/Perception rolls against Stealth (Ambush)/Agility to detect an ambush.'},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Watanu-Trained', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 1, 'cost_text': '1 pt', 'tags': [], 'effect': 'Select one Craft Skill related to metallic goods (not weapons or armor). +1k1 to Skill Rolls creating such items.'},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Way of the Land', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 2, 'cost_text': '2 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Select the lands of one family, a major city, or reasonably sized region. Cannot get lost there; know the location of all available resources. Unicorn pay 1 pt.'},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Wealthy', 'category': 'Material', 'points': 1, 'cost_text': '1 pt/Rank', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'For each point, gain 2 additional koku added to School Outfit starting amount. Crane, Unicorn, and Imperial pay 1 pt less total.'},
    {'kind': 'advantage', 'name': 'Well-Connected', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts/Rank', 'tags': [], 'effect': 'Choose one location where courts are held (a capital castle or a major city). Whenever a court session occurs at that location and you are present, you gain +10 disposition with every named character attending that court session. Additionally, once per OOC week per Rank in this Advantage, you learn one topic that was created or shared between two characters in secret at that location: information that was not made public. Courtiers pay 1 pt less per Rank. NPC Trigger Rule: An NPC with Well-Connected always attends court at their chosen location when able. The secret topic revealed each week is selected by the engine based on relevance to the NPC’s current primary objective. If no secret topics were generated at that location during the week, no intelligence is produced for that cycle.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Anachronism', 'category': '', 'points': 2, 'cost_text': '2 pts', 'tags': ['Mental/Social', 'IH'], 'effect': 'Out of touch with modern conventions. TN of all Artisan, Craft, and Social Skill Rolls increased by 5. Only returned spirits may take this.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Antisocial', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '2/4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Preference for solitude manifests as rudeness. 2 pts: -1k0 to all Social Skill Rolls. 4 pts: -1k1. Worth 1 additional pt to Crab.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Ascetic', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 2, 'cost_text': '2 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'No taste for material things. School Outfit includes only necessities. When awarded Glory, receive only half. Ascetic monk characters receive only one quarter. Worth 3 pts to Dragon or Monk.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Bad Eyesight', 'category': 'Physical', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': '-1k1 to all ranged attack rolls and Perception-based rolls.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Bad Fortune', 'category': 'Spiritual', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Some unpleasant fate awaits. Common forms: Secret Love (someone sabotages your romantic interests), Disfigurement (visible birthmark regarded as bad fortune), Evil Eye (discolored eye, people avoid your gaze), Allergy (rash from common substance), Lingering Misfortune (once per OOC month, the engine randomly selects a point during the month and begins watching for a roll that succeeds by less than 5; the first qualifying roll after that point is turned into an automatic failure. The character does not know when the misfortune will strike. The trigger point is randomized each month so it may fall early or late in the cycle), Unknown Enemy, Moto Curse (-1k0 to resist Taint; Unicorn only, worth 4 pts), Yogo Curse (destined to betray the one you love most; Scorpion Clan normally only, worth 4 pts).'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Bad Health', 'category': 'Physical', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Chronic medical condition. Earth Ring considered 1 Rank lower for Wound Ranks and resisting diseases.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Bitter Betrothal', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 2, 'cost_text': '2 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Unhappy arranged marriage. Mutual dislike causes difficulty with domestic and bureaucratic tasks. Worth 3 pts to Imperial characters.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Black Sheep', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Family is disgusted with you but has not made you ronin. At character generation, apply a permanent -40 disposition modifier from all named characters within your family and a permanent -20 disposition modifier from all named characters within your clan (outside your family). Characters outside your clan are unaffected. These modifiers are applied at generation and stack with any other clan or family baseline modifiers. The character is still a member of their clan and family in name: they have not been cast out: but they are treated with open contempt by their relatives and cold suspicion by their clanmates.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Blackmailed', 'category': 'Social', 'points': None, 'cost_text': 'Variable', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Someone knows a dark secret of yours and intends to make you pay. Cost equals your Status Rank. Periodic demands must be weighed against potential disgrace.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Blind', 'category': 'Physical', 'points': 6, 'cost_text': '6 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': '-3k3 to all ranged attack rolls. -1k1 to melee attacks. Base Armor TN = Reflexes + 5 (armor still adds normally). Water Ring considered 2 Ranks lower for Move Actions. Simple Move Actions require Athletics/Agility (TN 20) or fall Prone. May not make Perception rolls based on sight.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Bounty', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 6, 'cost_text': '2/4/6 pts', 'tags': [], 'effect': 'Price on your head. 2 pts (minor, 1-5 koku, local magistrates; ID roll TN 25). 4 pts (serious, 10-15 koku, Clan magistrates; ID roll TN 15). 6 pts (heinous, 20+ koku, all Clan magistrates; possible Tsuruchi bounty hunters; ID roll TN 10).'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Brash', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Short temper. When threatened or insulted, must roll Willpower + Honor Rank (TN 25) or attack immediately. Worth 4 pts to Lion.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': "Can't Lie", 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 2, 'cost_text': '2 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Psychologically incapable of lying. If someone in your presence tells a lie you know is untrue, must succeed at Willpower (TN 20) or immediately correct them.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Cast Out', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '1/3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Denounced by a monastic order. 1 pt: disapproval of a single temple. 3 pts: a major Brotherhood sect. Members of that sect treat your Glory Rank as Infamy.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Compulsion', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '2-4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Hopelessly compelled to partake in some activity. The compulsion subject is tagged at character creation (e.g. sake, gambling, temples). Base TN 15 Willpower roll to resist; TN increases by 5 per additional point (max TN 25 at 4 pts). Trigger: the Willpower roll fires whenever the character enters or is present at a location containing the compulsion subject. Common location tags: sake: any town or city; gambling: any court or marketplace; temples: any province with a temple. On failure, the character spends their next available action indulging the compulsion instead of pursuing their objective. NPC Trigger Rule: The engine rolls automatically on arrival at a tagged location. On failure, the NPC’s next tick action is consumed by the compulsion.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Consumed', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': None, 'cost_text': 'Varies', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Utterly consumed by a Shourido tenet. Worth 1 additional pt to Spider. Control (4 pts, -1k1 to Etiquette and Sincerity), Determination (6 pts, cannot spend Void Points to enhance die rolls), Insight (4 pts, must roll Willpower TN 20 or fall into reverie when using a chosen School Skill), Knowledge (4 pts, must roll Willpower TN 25 or study any new topic encountered), Perfection (5 pts, must call one extra Raise for no effect on every roll or it fails; 6 pts for Crane), Strength (5 pts, must call one extra Raise to use Called Shot/Feint/Disarm; -1k0 to Etiquette), Will (4 pts, -1k1 to Courtier and Temptation Skill Rolls).'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Contrary', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Compelled to weigh in on every debate or dispute. Whenever the character is present during a public debate, contested topic discussion, or argument between two or more characters, they must roll Willpower (TN = 5 × the highest Glory Rank among the participants in the debate). On failure, the character is compelled to publicly declare their position on the topic. This costs them a conversation action or court AP (consumed by the outburst, not available for other use), their stance on the topic becomes public knowledge (feeding into the Topic & Momentum system as support or opposition), and all characters present now know where they stand: characters who agree gain a small disposition bump, characters who disagree take a disposition hit. Additionally, the interjection is treated as a Breach of Etiquette, Minor on the Honor table: Ranks 0–2 lose 0 Honor points, Ranks 3–4 lose 1 point, Ranks 5–10 lose 2 points. Observant characters may infer the Contrary character’s primary objective from the declared position, functioning as a partial free Probe. Worth 4 pts to Imperial and courtier characters. NPC Trigger Rule: The engine rolls automatically whenever the Contrary NPC is present at a debate. On failure, the NPC declares the position most aligned with their primary objective.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Cursed by the Realm', 'category': 'Spiritual', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Marked as a foe by one spirit realm. Worth 5 pts to shugenja. Chikushudo: -1k1 to Animal Handling. Gaki-do: All gaki and hungry dead attack you first before any other target. Jigoku: -1k1 to rolls resisting Taint. Maigo no Musha: -1k1 to all rolls against any spirit. Meido: -1k0 to Perception rolls when unoccupied. Sakkaku: Once per in-game month, the engine rolls 1d20 on the Spirit Prank Table and applies the result. No repeats until all 20 pranks have been used, then the pool resets. Spirit Prank Table: 1: Misplaced Item (one random inventory item unavailable for 24 hours); 2: Loose Tongue (-1k0 to all Social Skill Rolls for 1 in-game week); 3: Void Drain (lose 1 Void Point at a random tick); 4: Noisy Shadow (-1k0 to all Stealth rolls for 1 in-game week); 5: Spoiled Provisions (lose 1 koku worth of food or supplies); 6: Fool’s Impression (-5 disposition with one random named character interacted with this month); 7: Stumble (next Athletics or movement roll suffers -1k1); 8: Smeared Ink (one outgoing letter delayed by 3 extra days); 9: Restless Night (one night this month, Void Points not recovered from rest); 10: Phantom Sounds (-1k0 to all Investigation (Notice) rolls for 1 in-game week); 11: Loose Straps (-5 to Armor TN for next combat encounter); 12: Whispered Embarrassment (lose 1 Glory point as embarrassing story circulates); 13: Unsettling Presence (-1k0 to all Willpower rolls for 1 in-game week); 14: Stuck Blade (first attack roll in next combat suffers -1k0); 15: Wrong Path (next travel action takes 1 extra in-game day); 16: Spilled Tea (automatic Breach of Etiquette, Minor at next formal social gathering with Honor loss per table); 17: Spooked Mount (next Horsemanship roll suffers -2k0); 18: Snapped String (-1k0 to next Perform or Kyujutsu roll); 19: Disrupted Kami (next spell casting roll suffers -1k0); 20: Tainted Gift (next gift given or received is perceived as slightly insulting, -3 disposition instead of normal bonus). Tengoku: +10 TN to all rolls while inside a temple devoted to the Celestial Heavens. Toshigoku: Must roll Willpower (TN 15) or attack any wounded opponent. Yomi: Cannot possess any Advantage or abilities referencing ancestral links. Yume-do: Require 10 hours of sleep to regain Void Points.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Dark Secret', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'A horrific secret that could ruin you and potentially others in your family. Exposure may require seppuku or execution. Worth 5 pts to ninja characters.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Debt', 'category': '', 'points': 8, 'cost_text': '2/4/8 pts', 'tags': ['Material/Social'], 'effect': '2 pts: debt of one quarter yearly stipend. 4 pts: debt of one full yearly stipend. 8 pts: debt substantially exceeding yearly stipend. Discovery causes Glory loss (at minimum one Rank); lord may disapprove. Creditor may leverage the debt for favors. Worth 1 additional pt to courtiers.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Disbeliever', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Faith in Rokugani theology has been shattered. If known publicly, shunned by the pious and expelled from temples and monastic orders. Social Skill Rolls with shugenja and monks have TN increased by +5.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Dishonored', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 5, 'cost_text': '5 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Name removed from family records. Most family members act as if you are dead. Status Rank 1 and cannot gain Status while this Disadvantage persists. May wash away dishonor by dying in battle (Deathseeker tradition).'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Disturbing Countenance', 'category': 'Physical', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Appearance causes concern and caution in others. TN of all Social Skill Rolls increased by +5. Worth 4 pts to Spider characters.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Doubt', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Something caused you to question your training. Select one School Skill. Every time you use it, must declare one Raise that confers no benefit.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Elemental Imbalance', 'category': 'Spiritual', 'points': 2, 'cost_text': '2 pts/Rank', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'A chosen element’s kami favor you too strongly. When casting a spell of that element, must roll Willpower (TN 15 + 5 per Rank of this Disadvantage). On failure, the element surges beyond control. The overflow effect depends on the element and scales with the Mastery Level (ML) of the spell being cast. Shugenja only; cannot choose an element you are already Deficient in.\nAir Overflow: the kami of wind strip away concealment and composure. ML 1–2: A sudden gust of shrieking wind erupts from the caster. All Stealth effects on the caster are broken and they cannot benefit from concealment for 1 hour. ML 3–4: The air around the caster becomes unnaturally still and transparent. Any Perceived Honor advantage the caster possesses fails for one in-game week and their true Honor Rank is visible to anyone making an Awareness roll (TN 10) in their presence. If the caster has no Perceived Honor, they suffer -1k1 to all Social Skill Rolls for one in-game week as their emotions and intentions become obvious. ML 5–6: A howling vortex erupts. All characters within 30 feet (including allies) must roll Air (TN 25) or be knocked Prone and pushed 10 feet in a random direction. The caster loses all remaining Air spell slots for the day. All ranged attacks originating from or targeting anyone within the affected area suffer -2k0 for 1 hour.\nEarth Overflow: the kami of stone overwhelm the caster’s body with rigidity. ML 1–2: The caster’s limbs stiffen. They cannot take Move Actions for 3 Rounds. ML 3–4: Partial petrification. The caster’s Water Ring is treated as 1 for movement and their Reflexes are reduced by 1 for 24 hours. ML 5–6: The ground buckles in a 20-foot radius. All characters in the area must roll Earth (TN 25) or be knocked Prone. The affected area becomes Difficult Terrain for 1 hour. The caster cannot cast any spell for 48 hours as the kami refuse to respond.\nFire Overflow: the kami of flame erupt beyond control. ML 1–2: The caster’s hands ignite. They take MLk1 Wounds and must drop anything held. ML 3–4: A ring of fire erupts around the caster. All characters within 10 feet (including allies) take MLk2 Wounds. The caster enters an involuntary Full Attack Stance for 2 Rounds. ML 5–6: Wildfire. The caster and all characters within 30 feet take MLk3 Wounds. All flammable equipment carried by affected characters has a 50% chance of being destroyed. The caster gains the Brash Disadvantage for one in-game week.\nWater Overflow: the kami of change overwhelm the caster’s form. ML 1–2: Water surges from the ground. The caster’s tile and all adjacent tiles become Moderate Terrain for 1 hour. The caster suffers -1k0 to their next Social Skill Roll (visibly drenched and disheveled). ML 3–4: The caster’s body becomes fluid and unstable. Agility and Reflexes are reduced by 1 for 24 hours. They suffer -1k0 to all attack rolls for the same duration. ML 5–6: A flash flood fills the area. All characters within 30 feet must roll Water (TN 25) or be swept 15 feet in a random direction and knocked Prone. The caster loses all remaining spell slots across all elements for the day. Any scrolls or paper items on the caster are destroyed.\nVoid Overflow: the kami of nothingness consume the caster’s spiritual connection. ML 1–2: The caster immediately loses 1 Void Point. If no Void Points remain, they take 5 Wounds instead. ML 3–4: All remaining Void Points are drained and cannot be recovered for 48 hours. The caster suffers -1k0 to all rolls for 24 hours. ML 5–6: Complete spiritual severance. All Void Points are lost. The caster cannot spend or recover Void Points for one in-game week and cannot cast Void spells for the same period. All characters within 10 feet experience a wave of existential dread (Fear 3 effect).'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Epilepsy', 'category': 'Physical', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Seizures triggered by high stress or flashing lights. Must roll Willpower (TN 15) to avoid. If failed, roll Willpower (TN 10) each minute to end the seizure. Worth 5 pts to Crane.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Failure of Bushido', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': None, 'cost_text': 'Varies', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'One tenet of Bushido is simply foreign to you. Worth 1 additional pt to ninja. Compassion (3 pts): must spend a Void Point before acting on behalf of someone of lower Status. Courage (4 pts): +5 TN to all rolls when facing a higher Glory/Status opponent or a Shadowlands opponent. Courtesy (4 pts): must call one no-effect Raise on Social rolls to apologize or avoid giving offense. Duty (6 pts): cannot spend Void Points to negate Wounds. Honesty (3 pts): cannot spend Void Points on Sincerity rolls where Honesty applies. Honor (3 pts): cannot add Honor Rank to rolls resisting Intimidation or Temptation. Sincerity (4 pts): must call one no-effect Raise on Sincerity conviction rolls or they automatically fail.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Forced Retirement', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Forced into early retirement into a monastery. May not advance further in current School. When gaining a new Insight Rank, must begin taking ranks of an unaligned Monk School (no Multiple Schools Advantage needed). Worth 5 pts to monk characters.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Frail Mind', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Difficulty concentrating. In any Contested Roll using Willpower, opponent gains +2k0.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Gaijin Name', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 1, 'cost_text': '1 pt', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'A name clearly not of Rokugani origin. Individual dice may only explode once on Social Skill Rolls (max die result: 20). Worth 2 pts to Unicorn.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Greedy', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Material wealth matters above all else. Opponents using Temptation (Bribery) gain +1k1 to their roll. Worth 4 pts to Mantis.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Gullible', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Trust given easily. Opponents using Sincerity (Deceit) against you gain +1k1 to their roll.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Hostage', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Exchanged as a guest during a Clan dispute resolution. Treated respectfully but may not leave without escort. Life forfeit if war breaks out between your Clan and hosts.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Idealistic', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 2, 'cost_text': '2 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Naively close adherence to Bushido. Impossible standards. When losing Honor, the loss is increased by 1 point. Worth 3 pts to Lion.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Infamous', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 2, 'cost_text': '2 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Known for ruthlessness and cruelty rather than valor. Starting Glory Rank is replaced with an Infamy Rank.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Insensitive', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 2, 'cost_text': '2 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': "Interested only in yourself. Must spend a Void Point to place yourself at risk for any other person's welfare unless there is an immediate personal benefit. Worth 3 pts to Scorpion."},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Jealousy', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Obsessed with outperforming one specific PC or major NPC. Will go to any lengths to best them. Once that target is bested, becomes jealous of someone else.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Lame', 'category': 'Physical', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'One leg is withered or near-useless. Water Ring considered 1 for Move Actions. Agility Trait Rolls or Agility-based Skill Rolls involving lower limbs suffer +10 TN.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Lechery', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 2, 'cost_text': '2 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Physical pleasure is a weakness. Opponents using Temptation (Seduction) against you gain +1k0 to the roll, provided the opponent’s gender matches your attraction (per orientation field, Section 22.3).'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Lost Love', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'A bond of true love has been lost to death. At character creation, record: Lost Love [Name], [Clan/Family], [Location of death]. When reminded of this loss, all TNs increase by 5 until a Void Point is spent to regain focus. Cannot trigger more than twice per in-game day; at least one hour between instances. Trigger: the reminder check fires when the character has a direct social interaction with a member of the lost love’s Clan or Family (conversation, court attendance together, receiving a letter), or when the character enters the province or city where the death occurred. NPC Trigger Rule: The engine rolls the trigger automatically. If the NPC has no Void Points to spend, the +5 TN penalty persists until Void Points are recovered.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Low Pain Threshold', 'category': 'Physical', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'TN penalties from Wound Ranks are increased by +5 per Rank.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Member of the Chrysanthemum Court', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 5, 'cost_text': '5 pts', 'tags': [], 'effect': 'Regular attendee at a cruel or capricious lord’s court. Failing a Social Skill Roll by more than 10 in that court permanently loses 5 Status Points + 1 per Raise declared. Status dropping to 0 = executed.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Missing Limb', 'category': 'Physical', 'points': 6, 'cost_text': '6 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'One limb is missing. +10 TN to all tasks involving the missing limb (e.g.\xa0wielding a two-handed weapon with one arm). Rolls not involving that limb (e.g.\xa0running) are unaffected.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Momoku', 'category': 'Spiritual', 'points': 8, 'cost_text': '8 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Fundamental spiritual imbalance. Possess Void Points but may not spend them on anything except School Techniques which specifically require them.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Obligation', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 6, 'cost_text': '3/6 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'You owe a favor to a specific named character. 3 pts: a minor favor: the creditor may call on you for a small task or concession. 6 pts: a major favor: the creditor may demand significant action, resources, or political support. NOT AVAILABLE AT CHARACTER CREATION: may only be acquired during play through events, debts, or narrative consequences.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Obtuse', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Fine things simply escape you. XP cost to increase any High Skill other than Investigation or Medicine is doubled. Worth 4 pts to Crab and bushi.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Overconfident', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Grossly inflated view of own prowess. When outnumbered or facing a clearly superior enemy, must succeed at Perception (TN 20) to recognize the situation and withdraw rather than engage. Worth 4 pts to Lion and Mantis.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Permanent Wound', 'category': 'Physical', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'First Wound Rank is always considered full. Worth 5 pts to bushi.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Phobia', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '1-3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Irrational, uncontrollable fear. When confronted with the subject, all TNs increased by +5 per point possessed in this Disadvantage. At character creation, record: Phobia [Subject] with associated situation tags. The TN penalty applies whenever the character is in a situation matching the tags. Common phobias and their tags: fire: combat involving Fire spells, burning structures, large open flames; heights: castle walls, mountain terrain, bridges, cliff paths; water: naval travel, river crossings, heavy rain combat; the Shadowlands: Shadowlands-adjacent provinces, Tainted zones; spiders: Shinomen Forest, Shadowlands encounters with spider creatures; crowds: any court in session, major city marketplaces. The penalty persists for the duration of the character’s presence in the tagged situation. NPC Trigger Rule: The engine applies the TN penalty automatically whenever the NPC enters a tagged situation. NPCs with Phobia will avoid tagged locations when possible, treating them as a negative weight in pathfinding and objective pursuit.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Rumormonger', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Cannot resist spreading rumors. When presented with an opportunity, must roll Willpower (TN = 5 × highest involved person’s Glory Rank) or spread the rumor. Worth 5 pts to courtier characters.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': "Seven Fortunes' Curse", 'category': 'Spiritual', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'One of the Seven Fortunes has found your behavior unacceptable. Benten’s Curse: +10 TN to all Etiquette rolls. Bishamon’s Curse: Strength considered 1 Rank lower for weapon Damage Rolls. Daikoku’s Curse: -1k1 to Commerce rolls; starting koku reduced by 1. Ebisu’s Curse: -1k1 to Social Skill Rolls with non-samurai Rokugani. Fukurokujin’s Curse: +5 TN to Lore Skill Rolls. Hotei’s Curse (6 pts): Any Technique or Advantage requiring a Void Point now costs two Void Points. Jurojin’s Curse: -2k0 to resist all poisons and diseases.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Shadowlands Taint', 'category': 'Spiritual', 'points': 4, 'cost_text': '4 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'You have felt the touch of darkness. Possess 0.5 Ranks of Shadowlands Taint. May not be detectable at this level. See Section 42 for full Taint rules.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Sleeper Agent', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 5, 'cost_text': '5 pts', 'tags': [], 'effect': 'The Kolat previously kidnapped and programmed you. A trigger word or phrase followed by a command of 5 words or less compels you to carry out the command regardless of personal wishes. Worth 8 pts if a fail-safe causing self-destruction on mission failure is included. NOT AVAILABLE AT CHARACTER CREATION: applied only by the engine during world generation or through Kolat conditioning events during play. Full activation mechanics, conditioning stability, and execution model are defined in Section 54.7e (Kolat Sleeper Agent Activation Mechanics).'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Small', 'category': 'Physical', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Noticeably smaller than average. Water Ring considered 1 Rank lower for Move Action distance. -1k0 to Damage Rolls for all melee attacks. Cannot take the Large Advantage.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Social Disadvantage', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Slipped from position in the Celestial Order. Begin with Status Rank 0.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Soft-Hearted', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 2, 'cost_text': '2 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Human life is precious to you. When facing the opportunity to kill a human being, must roll Willpower (TN 20) or be unable to do so. If you do kill, all TNs increased by +10 for one day. Worth 3 pts to Phoenix.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Sworn Enemy', 'category': 'Social', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'An enemy who will stop at nothing to see you defeated or killed. Base cost assumes equal Insight Rank; +1 pt per Insight Rank above yours the enemy possesses. For +2 pts, the enemy becomes your kharmic nemesis and you may not spend Void Points when opposing them.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Touch of the Void', 'category': 'Spiritual', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Touched by the Void; using it can overwhelm you. When spending a Void Point to augment a roll, gain +2k1 instead of +1k1. Each time a Void Point is spent, must roll Willpower (TN 30) or be Dazed for one Round. Worth 4 pts to Phoenix.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'True Love', 'category': 'Mental', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'At character creation, record: True Love [Named Character]. Any time the character takes an action that would negatively affect the lover: causing a disposition drop with the lover, harming or opposing the lover’s clan, working against the lover’s objectives, attacking the lover’s allies, or any other action that would reduce the lover’s wellbeing: the character must spend a Void Point before taking that action. If no Void Points are available, the character cannot take the action that tick. NPC Trigger Rule: The engine checks each action against the lover’s character record. If the action would produce any negative consequence for the lover, the Void Point cost is applied automatically. NPCs with True Love will avoid actions that harm their lover when low on Void Points.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Uncentered', 'category': 'Spiritual', 'points': 2, 'cost_text': '2 pts for Clan Monks, 4 pts for Brotherhood Monks', 'tags': [], 'effect': 'Cannot learn any Void Kiho. Cannot take the Ishiken-do or Void Versatility Advantages.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Wanderer', 'category': '', 'points': 2, 'cost_text': '2 pts', 'tags': [], 'effect': '-15 penalty when using the Navigation Emphasis. Gets lost easily even in familiar areas without a guide.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Weakness', 'category': 'Physical', 'points': 6, 'cost_text': '6 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Select one Trait. That Trait is treated as 1 Rank lower for all rolls and Trait-based mechanical effects.'},
    {'kind': 'disadvantage', 'name': 'Wrath of the Kami', 'category': 'Spiritual', 'points': 3, 'cost_text': '3 pts', 'tags': ['CR'], 'effect': 'Spirits of one element (chosen at purchase) vehemently dislike you. Spells of that element cast against you confer one Free Raise on the Spell Casting Roll. Worth 4 pts to shugenja.'},
